    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Prol.">
        <head>VI Atr Lat Prol.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-k">Quodam tempore contiget, ut regis Æþelredi edicto concrepante, archipresulumque Ælfeahi et Þulfstani hortatu instigante, uniuersi Anglorum optimates die sancto pentecosten ad locum ab indigenis Eanham nominatum acciti sunt conuenire.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Latin paraphrase of VI Atr (early 11th c.; K = Cotton Claudius A III f. 30). This passage has no Old English equivalent; Liebermann gives no German translation.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
